#TETHERVERSE FRONTEND — LOCAL OVERRIDES
#
# Nothing here needs to be set.
#
#   `.env` (committed)   the two public origins a build cannot run without.
#   wrangler.toml        the backend address, read at runtime by the Worker.
#
# This file is the reference for the knobs that are personal to one machine, and
# for the shape of a value if you need to override one. Copy it to `.env.local`
# (ignored by git), which outranks `.env`.
#
# There is no secret in this app: it holds no database credentials and forwards
# its API routes to the Tetherverse API, which owns the schema. The one value
# that could be considered sensitive is the backend address, and it lives in the
# Worker configuration rather than here.

# ── Dev-server origin allowlist ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Local development only, comma-separated. Next 16 blocks cross-origin dev
# resources (the HMR websocket, font preloads) by default; listing an origin is
# what lets a phone on the LAN load http://192.168.1.15:3000 cleanly.
#
# Empty in production: only the deployed Worker should be loading this app.
ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=

# ── Backend, for a local run ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `next dev` already falls back to http://localhost:4000, so this is only needed
# to point a local build or a `next start` at a deployed API. Leave it commented
# in `.env.local` unless you mean it: OpenNext copies the env files it finds into
# the Worker as defaults, and a stale address baked in that way outranks nothing
# but is easy to forget about.
#
#   TETHERVERSE_API_URL=https://tetherverse-backend-46039623481.asia-southeast1.run.app

# ── Public origins, for reference ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set in the committed `.env`. They are inlined into the client at build time,
# so overriding one here means the Worker you build is no longer the one the
# launcher is allowed to frame.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_EXCEL_AUTH_FRONTEND_URL=https://auth.excelmec.org
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCHER_ORIGIN=https://play.excelmec.org
